Libraries & Technologies Used

 1. Python
Python is the main programming language used to develop this project. It is used for data cleaning, data analysis, calculations, and generating useful insights from mobile app usage data.

 2. Pandas
Pandas is used for data manipulation and analysis. It helps in loading CSV files, handling missing values, removing duplicate records, filtering data, grouping users, and analyzing mobile app usage.

 3. NumPy
NumPy is used for numerical calculations and statistical analysis. It helps calculate the mean, median, standard deviation, and identify unusual session durations.

 4. CSV (Comma-Separated Values)
CSV is used as the dataset file format for storing and accessing mobile app usage records, including session duration, app features, device information, ratings, and user details.

 5. Visual Studio Code (VS Code)
VS Code is used as the development environment for writing, executing, testing, and managing the Python project files.

6. Git & GitHub
Git is used for version control and tracking project changes. GitHub is used to store, manage, and share the project source code and output files online.

## Project Overview

Mobile App Usage & User Engagement Analysis is a Python-based data analysis project that focuses on understanding how users interact with mobile applications. It analyzes session duration, app features, user ratings, device types, age groups, and usage patterns to gain meaningful insights into user behavior.

## Project Objectives

- Analyze mobile application usage patterns.
- Identify the most frequently used application features.
- Calculate average user session duration.
- Compare usage across different devices.
- Analyze user engagement levels.
- Identify peak usage hours and busiest weekdays.
- Evaluate user ratings for application features.
- Generate data-driven recommendations

